course: dictionary
lesson: 2534
title: Deeply: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Deeply» is a good example. Its meaning changes with the words around it, so always check the sentence before you decide.
explain: «A girl cut her hand deeply and needed stitches.» Here deeply means far in, into the skin. Try your meaning in the sentence: far in makes sense, so that is the right one. In «deeply cruel», though, deeply means very much: the cruelty is strong, not a place.
explain: Look at the word that comes before deeply. «Breathe deeply» means fully and slowly, the way you breathe to calm down when you feel angry or scared. «Think deeply» means thinking hard and carefully. «Deeply sorry» means very much sorry. The clues always tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Deeply is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done or how much. Its forms are deeply, more deeply and most deeply.
fact: «Deeply» can mean very much or strongly, as in «deeply sorry» and «hurt deeply».
fact: «Deeply» can mean far down or far in, as in «roots go deeply into the soil».
fact: «Deeply» can mean fully and slowly, as in «breathe deeply» or «sleep deeply».
fact: «Deeply» can also mean thinking hard and carefully, as in «think deeply» about a problem.
exercise: «A girl cut her hand deeply and needed stitches.» What does deeply mean here? | Slowly and calmly | Thinking hard | *Far in, into the skin | Very happily
exercise: Mia says, «Sit still and breathe deeply.» What does deeply mean? | Very loudly | *Fully and slowly | Quickly and with a rush | Far under the water
exercise: «Pranks that trick someone and then laugh at them are deeply cruel.» What does deeply mean? | *Very much, strongly | Carefully, after thinking | Slowly and softly | Far down
test: «Ravi was deeply sorry for breaking the vase.» What does deeply mean? | Under the ground | *Very much | Quietly | Thinking carefully for a long time
test: Mum says, «Please think deeply before you answer.» What does deeply mean? | Far below the ground | Very loudly | Very fast | *Thinking hard and carefully
exam: What does deeply mean in «roots go deeply into the soil»? | Fully and slowly | *Far down | Thinking hard | Very much
